WEBVTT

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.980
I found the first star of the evening!

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.190
Aww, you beat me to it...

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.230
We used to search for it all the time, huh?

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.730
I found it more often.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.490
Huh? No, I did.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.160
I wonder how many engine fragments are left.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.460
Hmm, come to think of it...

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.370
He hasn't told you?

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.170
What if he said a hundred are left?

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.800
If there are that many, it'll be rough.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.010
You sound kind of happy about it.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:42.310
Well, if that were the case, we could stay
magic users together for a while longer...

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.270
What's that?

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.110
A band of light?

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:00.370
No... Not yet. It's too soon.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.550
After-School Pleiades

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.720
Sobbingly, I went on my journey

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:27.190
Wishing I could at least fly through the sky

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:33.570
And yet the stars gently shone on me in the nights after our quarrels

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:39.120
I wonder if you were also watching them

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:44.370
I don't know... I want to know... I want to feel it...

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:51.420
Nothingness simply means there are infinite possibilities

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.210
The excitement I got after realizing that

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:58.300
was like surfing the waves of space and time

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:03.390
How strange that I'm not afraid anymore

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:06.100
Let's embrace our imperfections and go on

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.980
We'll open the promised door

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:14.150
and gain dazzling smiles!

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.590
Everyone, can you see it?

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.510
You mean this sky?

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.300
Yes, this. President, do you know anything?

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.800
It's pretty, but a little scary.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.600
Yes. Could you gather in the club room again?

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:45.600
Again?

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.480
What on Earth is that?

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.600
I wonder if other people can see it.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.360
No, they can't.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.980
So it does have something to do with you?

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.570
You all, as well. This is our spaceship.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.660
This is?

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.610
What does this mean?

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.200
The time limit is drawing near!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:09.620
Flower of Awakening

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.140
The meteor shower forecast!

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.680
Why, at a time like this?

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:25.890
No, it's the perfect time.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:29.270
Right now, we need as many
engine fragments as possible.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.650
Wasn't that star the spaceship?

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.030
Long ago, after losing our home,

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:42.030
we set off on an aimless journey,
searching for a new land.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.030
But we found that space was
far too vast to traverse.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.950
So we used a certain method.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.040
Magic? You mean magic, right?

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.920
We possess the technology to
select our desired outcome,

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.170
out of all the possibilities in the universe.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.970
No matter how unlikely the odds,
as long as it isn't zero,

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.100
we can seize it, in exchange for vast energy.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.470
That isn't magic?

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:08.930
It's magic enough.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.390
You said that about us before, too.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:16.650
However, there was no
chance left for us to survive.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:21.400
So the option we chose was not choosing.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.650
Not choosing?

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:27.700
Living means constantly making choices.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.580
So, because we refused to choose,

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.910
we became life forms that
exist outside the universe.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:39.420
Thus, we effectively froze time and
began a journey that might never end.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.550
What you're seeing now is only
a faint remnant of our ship.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.510
I don't really get it, but that sounds reckless.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.600
I don't know how much time passed after that.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.640
But seven Earth years ago,

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:58.150
just as we were approaching Earth,
there was an accident.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.150
The engine fell apart, and without its power source,

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:05.530
our spaceship began losing its ability
to escape the laws of space.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:06.910
Seven years ago?

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.410
You mean...

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:12.580
Anyway, right now, we need to gather
the fragments and repair the engine!

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.590
This is a spaceship?

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.090
Hey, how many more fragments are there?

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.840
By my estimation, there are twelve fragments.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:33.100
No, the first one we obtained split, so thirteen?

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:37.310
We have five, and that dark boy has three.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.360
Then there are five more?

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.360
That's fewer than I expected.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.030
We'd be in trouble if there were lots!

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.610
Looks like he isn't showing up tonight.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.320
That's perfect. Let's finish this quickly!

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.540
Go on, Subaru.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:56.410
Yeah.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.510
Let's head back to the club room, Subaru.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:09.680
Oh, sure.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:19.850
What are you doing?

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:22.650
As you can see, I'm rebuilding the engine.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:23.770
Rebuilding?

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.940
This will let me restart the spaceship.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.450
But you don't have all the pieces, right?

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:32.240
Our engine was designed at the
elementary-particle level.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.450
Even fragmented, it can still
function to some degree.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.460
So, how long will this take?

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.960
A while longer. I think this is enough for today.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.710
It'd be so much easier if
things always went like this.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.710
It usually is pretty easy, isn't it?

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.220
Huh? My English notebook is missing...

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.840
You were doing your homework
in the club room, right?

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.720
Oh, yeah. I need to go back and get it.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.470
If you've finished your homework,
can't it wait until tomorrow?

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.680
Yeah, but...

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.100
I'll wait for you at the gate.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:19.250
That's...

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.580
the fragment I captured with Aoi-chan.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.540
But that guy took it from us...

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:28.210
Why is it here?

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:37.100
This...

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.610
What was that sound?

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.660
We transformed!

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:54.700
What does this mean?

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.450
The safety device activated!

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:58.790
Something's happened in the club room!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:00.660
Subaru?

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:10.670
Everyone!

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:12.970
Move, Subaru!

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:14.300
Huh?

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.930
Huh? The window won't open.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:18.640
Why?

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:21.140
Everyone! I've seen today's fragment before!

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:24.520
Remember? The one that was taken
after Aoi-chan and I captured it.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.230
What do you mean?

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.020
It couldn't be...

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:33.400
This magic circle...

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.530
Horned Cape?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:35.950
Of course! Curses!

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:36.530
Huh?

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:40.290
He found our location by making us
bring his own fragment back here!

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.960
We've fallen into his trap.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.000
He used his own fragment as bait?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.330
Everyone here is so reckless!

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.040
But right now, the spaceship....

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:52.300
Yeah, but I don't think this is a coincidence.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.630
He can't afford to be choosy, either.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:56.340
Cosplay Research Club

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:56.340
Please knock!

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:56.340
No opening when we're changing!

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.060
He shouldn't be able to find it that easily.

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.060
What should I do?

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:09.190
It doesn't matter which!
Just open a window and let us in!

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.570
Okay, I'll try.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:11.820
Wait, Subaru.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:12.860
Huh?

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.360
He's probably inside, as well. Be careful.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:18.240
If you see him, run.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:19.870
Okay.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:20.740
Cosplay Research Club

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.140
No good here, either...

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.940
All the teachers are gone, too.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.740
Oh, sorry—

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.200
G-Good evening...

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.200
Magic user, why are you here?

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.620
No, this is perfect.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.160
Tell me where the fragments are.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.250
Wait!

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.670
What do I do?!

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.630
Th-The observatory!

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.720
M-My transformation...

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.730
S-S-Stop!

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.690
You're full of energy, Subaru.

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:32.860
Minato-kun...

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.190
Th-Thank you.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.570
What's the matter?

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:37.820
Th-There's big trouble!

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:39.910
Everyone's locked in...

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:43.120
Er, I'm the one locked in,

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:46.000
b-but at this rate, all the
fragments we gathered are...

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.960
Fragments? Of what?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.210
I never can understand what you're talking about.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:58.380
Don't force it.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:02.470
No good. It won't open anywhere...

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:07.100
What will happen if we can't restart the spaceship?

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:12.610
That ring of light is a tiny part of the
spaceship that's beginning to materialize.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:16.610
Soon, the entire ship will materialize,

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.320
and all my sleeping comrades will wake.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.490
Would that be bad?

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:24.160
Yes, that would be the worst outcome of all.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:41.430
Subaru, what's in your pocket?

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:42.260
Huh?

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:47.470
I picked this up in our club room earlier.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:51.520
It looks like yours, but it's not, is it?

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:54.900
Minato-kun?

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:58.650
I'm sorry! I left the door open!

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.900
No, it's not that...

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:02.400
Come to the nurse's office!

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:06.410
More importantly, you want to
see your friends, don't you?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:13.000
If the stars led you here,

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.000
then perhaps it's time I
answered their call, as well.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:23.510
Besides, I'm interested in these friends
who seem to keep troubling you.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:27.300
Continue down this path, as far as it goes.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.260
Don't look elsewhere.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.060
You should find what you seek in there.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:36.810
What should I do? I can't make this decision.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.440
But you must decide.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.320
I'll be all right.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:42.820
But...

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.240
You're hopeless, Subaru.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.790
This'll protect you.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.540
You once invited me, didn't you?

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:55.710
Huh?

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.790
To go see the stars with you.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:00.840
Oh... The first time we met.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.420
But you turned me down.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:05.510
I only asked you why.

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:08.930
It had been a very long time
since anyone had asked me that.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:11.470
I see.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:15.440
Will you invite me again someday?

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:17.190
Sure.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.820
Now, have you decided?

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:25.110
I'm going.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:33.290
But when you leave this place,
I'll take you to the nurse's office first!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:40.420
I've never even thought of leaving here...

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.090
Subaru...

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:47.050
Can I change, too?

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:52.970
This is...

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:07.070
What is this place?

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.500
A door...

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.130
Look! What's that?

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:32.140
The door to the observatory is glowing!

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:35.890
Subaru!

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:35.890
Subaru-chan!

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:37.270
Everyone!

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:39.390
You did it, Subarun!

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:41.980
You're amazing.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.940
Huh? This is the observatory?

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.070
There's no time! We must hurry and stop him!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.820
Subaru, transform.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.070
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.120
Where are the fragments?

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.910
Hold it!

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:57.700
Found you.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:00.330
You Horned Cape! Why are you here?

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.090
We won't give our fragments to you!

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:10.720
Whoa!

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:12.470
We did it! We drove him off!

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:16.850
I'll go to the club room and
hurry to rebuild the engine.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.020
Everyone, hold him off until I finish.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:19.940
Got it!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:25.190
Huh?

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:26.860
This is...

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:27.440
Our school is...

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.650
What's going on?

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:31.950
What did you do?

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.830
What are you planning to do?

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:39.080
I told you.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:41.960
I'll take them by force.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.840
He's planning to force his way through.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:45.630
Use the magic circle!

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:50.340
The school building!

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:51.470
I can't believe him!

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:59.390
The club room...

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.140
President?

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.390
I found them.

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:06.980
Now, hand them over.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:08.530
No!

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.860
We collected all of these together.

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.490
We'll never let you have them!

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:14.490
Don't blame me for what happens, then.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:15.490
Aoi...

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:16.620
Aoi-chan?

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.240
Damn, my shaft....

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:21.210
Jeez, why does this always happen?

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:24.080
Wait... Subaru? Where's Subaru?

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.630
Subaru? What are you doing?

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.380
I won't hand over the fragments.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:30.760
I won't let you destroy our school.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.380
And I won't let you hurt Aoi-chan!

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:36.390
Are you not afraid doing that?

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:39.720
I am afraid... Very afraid.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:41.520
But that doesn't matter!

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.230
Subaru, move!

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:44.600
I won't!

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:50.610
Huh?

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.240
The fragments...

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.080
It's started!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:10.090
What?

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.340
This light...

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:13.090
Space is glowing?

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:19.930
There's no time! I'm starting the engine!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:21.600
Did you finish repairing the engine?

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.100
I haven't, but I have to do it anyway.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:26.310
The spaceship has started materializing.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.730
That's what this is?

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:30.610
I can't believe it was this close.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.190
What should we do?

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:35.610
Everyone, use your drive shafts as spark plugs.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:38.030
You can say that, but our shafts are—

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.210
Floor the accelerator!

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:47.750
It's all or nothing now!

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:58.800
It's not starting?

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:01.930
There's not enough energy!

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:04.100
Hold on, isn't this...

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.060
...too big?

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:07.940
It's falling...

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.810
It'll hit Earth!

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:13.320
These aliens need their engine's power.

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:15.940
Don't you care what happens to them?

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:17.950
I do not.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:21.450
In a different sense, he's as hard
to level with as the president!

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.290
Subaru, you're shaking.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:33.340
Please... Move...

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:57.530
Huh? Our shafts...

00:18:57.820 --> 00:18:58.900
They changed.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.410
Why?

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:41.570
Where am I?

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.450
Who are you?

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:48.500
Welcome.

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:51.040
But now I have to go.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:53.460
This place will close soon.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.960
Who are you?

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:57.670
Who am I?

00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.210
I'm...

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:04.090
The spaceship is disappearing.

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.560
Did it work?

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:07.970
I think so.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:16.360
This is...

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:20.900
It's the president!

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:23.610
The fragments are also back! Wait...

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:25.950
One, two, three...

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:26.950
There are eight of them!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:31.960
Yeah, all the fragments that boy stole
have returned to us, as well.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:34.710
So these are all the fragments we've found?

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:38.210
Yes! Thank you, everyone, for helping us!

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:41.880
Well, at this point, it's not
like we can stay out of it.

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:44.510
There really was a spaceship.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:47.220
I never heard anything about it being so big.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:51.270
Most of the ship has been shifted
to a higher dimension,

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:53.020
so we should be safe for a while.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:56.690
However, I'll need the remaining
five fragments of the engine

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:59.650
to truly repair the spaceship's functions.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:03.280
Looks like we still have a long way to go...

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:22.210
No...

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:40.520
Minato-kun...

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:44.820
We'll see each other again, right?

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:50.030
To Be Continued

00:21:57.210 --> 00:22:01.670
You see, when I looked up

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:07.050
everyone was smiling at me

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:16.770
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:25.740
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:23.110
...my daily life...

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:35.500
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:37.370
"Can I fly?"

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:41.580
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:22:41.580 --> 00:22:47.220
We can go there whenever we want to

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:56.890
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:22:56.890 --> 00:23:01.520
"We have to catch them!"

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:06.030
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:11.360
the scenery around us glittered

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:16.080
sometime after school

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:22.920
The shafts changed shape?

00:23:22.920 --> 00:23:24.960
I've been tweaking mine for a while.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:27.710
It means that you're growing, too.

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:34.970
Next Episode
Two Treasures, or The Smell of Strawberries

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:31.510
Two Treasures, or
The Smell of Strawberries.

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:32.840
Which is it?
